A||N||4||perks88gt||A/C and stalling...||||5||
Z||000000||perks88gt||04-25-2001||06:36 PM||||I have owned 1 87 GT and 2 88 GT's in the past 8 years.  All three cars have experienced stalling while using the air conditioner.  The condition usualy occured during long-term high way use, or during a very hot day in the city.  My father has owned 4 GT's and has experienced the same problem, so I can only conclude that this is a typical problem with V6 fiero's, does anyone have a solution?? ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Wade87GT||04-25-2001||07:12 PM||||I've driven (pretty hard, most of the time) my 87 GT almost daily for 12 years/140,000+ miles and can't recall that ever happening to me. I'm leaning towards a high temp problem for you though. I've also been using an 160 degree thermostat and fan switch for several years now. It never runs hot and I'm glad it doesn't stay cold very long in the winter, because it doesn't put out enough heat.<P>Wade||||reg||14
Z||000002||Carrolles||04-26-2001||07:50 AM||||Neither my 85SE v-6 nor my 85GT have this problem.  I do notice the drop in rpms when the compressor kicks in but it is not enough to stall the engine.<P>The ecm actually raises the rpms slightly about 1/2 second before it allows the a/c clutch to engage.<P>Do the engines run ok otherwise?  Maybe its time for de-carbonizing.||||reg||1
Z||000003||perks88gt||04-26-2001||11:23 AM||||All three cars I drove with this problem have been in imaculate running condition.  I used that D-carb stuff back on my 87, with no great result.  The cars are not running "to hot", there still under the half way mark on the temp guage in city traffic.  <BR>||||reg||9
Z||000004||theogre||04-26-2001||07:45 PM||||Did you try resetting the timing? That's one thing that could cause it. It may seem to be running great but if the distributor is off it could be enough that the ECM can't cope when the AC is on. It would not take a big error to be a problem.<P>With the frequency of EGR problems I'd look for even small problems developing there.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 04-26-2001).]||||reg||1
